language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ A heterosquare of order n: the n by n square holds the distinct integers 1 to n*n, and its row, column and diagonal sums are all different.
given n : int
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..n*n)
find sums : matrix indexed by [int(1..2*n+2)] of int(0..n*n*n)

branching on [x]

such that
$ the square holds the distinct integers 1 to n*n
allDiff(flatten(x)),
$ the first 2n entries of sums are the row sums and the column sums
forAll i : int(1..n) . sums[i] = (sum j : int(1..n) . x[i,j]),
forAll j : int(1..n) . sums[n+j] = (sum i : int(1..n) . x[i,j]),
$ the next two entries of sums are the two diagonal sums
sums[2*n+1] = (sum i : int(1..n) . x[i,i]),
sums[2*n+2] = (sum i : int(1..n) . x[i,n+1-i]),
$ the row, column and diagonal sums must all be different
allDiff(sums)
